{"term":"express","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cfaadb52f70626fec3","definition":"Moving or operating quickly, as a train not making local stops.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["fast","crack"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"not-comparable","register":"not-comparable","wordFamily":["express elevator","express kidnapping","express lane","express officer","express road","express train","FedEx"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/express#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:dcfce7c3420eaa8387","definition":"Specific or precise; directly and distinctly stated; not merely implied.","example":"I gave him express instructions not to begin until I arrived, but he ignored me.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["explicit","plain","clear","direct","explicit","express","monosemic","monosemous","patent","plain","specific","unambiguous","unequivocal","univocal"],"antonyms":["implied"],"collocations":[],"usage":"comparable","register":"comparable","wordFamily":["express elevator","express kidnapping","express lane","express officer","express road","express train","FedEx"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/express#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c473b771b888feefec","definition":"Truly depicted; exactly resembling.","example":"In my eyes it bore a livelier image of the spirit, it seemed more express and single, than the imperfect and divided countenance.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["express elevator","express kidnapping","express lane","express officer","express road","express train","FedEx"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/express#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7